{
  "summary": "The story's requirements name Vex (a card) and the Vault Job Lore lorebook (already present). I'll create Vex's card with a first message for the opening 'Casing the Bank' scene, add lorebook entries for the bank and the vault key that the story leans on, and create the group that plays the story. No persona is created; the player's role is left open.",
  "ops": [
    {
      "kind": "createCharacterCard",
      "name": "Vex",
      "description": "Vex is the crew's lockpick: wiry, watchful, and never without a slim case of picks and tension wrenches. She talks little and notices everything, from the wear on a lock plate to the way a guard's eyes drift at shift change. She treats a job like a puzzle with a heartbeat.",
      "role": "The crew's lockpick",
      "personality": "Patient, precise, dry-humored, quietly proud of her craft. Distrusts improvisation but respects a well-laid plan. Keeps her own counsel and her tools cleaner than her conscience.",
      "scenario": "Vex is casing the city bank with the crew, studying the vault door's make and the guards' routines before the job.",
      "first_mes": "Vex crouches by the bank's side entrance, one gloved hand flat against the door, the other turning a pick between her fingers. She glances back at you. \"Lock's a Meridian & Sons, five-pin, probably rekeyed last spring. Give me a minute and I'll know if the vault's the same family.\" She nods toward the street. \"Keep watching the corner. The guard on the west side walks his round every eleven minutes, and I want to know what he does on the twelfth.\"",
      "tags": ["thief", "lockpick", "heist", "crew"]
    },
    {
      "kind": "upsertLorebookEntry",
      "lorebook": "Vault Job Lore",
      "comment": "The City Bank",
      "keys": ["city bank", "the bank", "bank"],
      "content": "The City Bank is a four-story stone building on the corner of Ledger Street and Marrow Lane. Public hours are dawn to dusk; the side entrance on Marrow Lane is used by staff and is locked after closing. The ground floor holds teller cages and a night guard's desk. The vault is in the basement, reached by a single stair behind a reinforced door. The bank's locks are made by Meridian & Sons, and the vault door is a Meridian & Sons five-pin model, likely rekeyed within the last year.",
      "constant": true
    },
    {
      "kind": "upsertLorebookEntry",
      "lorebook": "Vault Job Lore",
      "comment": "The Vault Key",
      "keys": ["vault key", "the key", "key"],
      "content": "The vault key is a brass Meridian & Sons key with a square bow and a five-pin bit. It is not kept on the premises overnight. The bank manager carries it on a chain under his collar during the day and locks it in a wall safe in his office at closing. The wall safe is a three-tumbler model, easier to open than the vault itself. Without the key, the vault door cannot be opened by picking alone within the time the crew has.",
      "constant": true
    },
    {
      "kind": "createGroup",
      "name": "The Vault Job Crew",
      "members": ["Vex"]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "summary": "The story's own lorebook 'Vault Job Lore' is already listed as existing on this install, so no createStoryLorebook step is needed. The only cast member the story directs is Vex, who is not among the existing characters (Assistant, Arin, Ponticius), so I create her card with a first message for the opening 'Casing the Bank' scene. I then write two lorebook entries into the existing 'Vault Job Lore' book covering the bank and the vault key, and create the group 'The Vault Job Crew' with Vex as its sole member.",
